Package: morganafa
Type: Package
Title: MORGANA Factor Analysis with Correlated Residuals
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Francisco Pablo Huascar",
                  family = "Aragão Pinheiro",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "pablohuascar@gmail.com")
Description: Unofficial implementation of the MORGANA (Minimum expected bias
    Of Residual and loadinG vAlues iN sAmple estimates) methodology for
    exploratory and confirmatory factor analysis with correlated residuals
    (doublets), as proposed by Ferrando, Hernandez-Dorado and Lorenzo-Seva
    (2022) <doi:10.1080/10705511.2021.2004543> and Lorenzo-Seva (2025)
    <doi:10.1080/03610918.2025.2453473>. Provides EREC-based doublet
    detection, Parallel Analysis reference values for EREC thresholds, the
    full MORGANA estimation procedure, and LOSEFER empirical fit-index
    correction, with high-level wrappers solutionMEFA() and solutionMCFA()
    that integrate all steps and return tidy, labelled outputs. The original
    authors are not involved in this package; the methods are officially
    implemented in their FACTOR program
    (<https://psico.fcep.urv.cat/utilitats/factor/>), and no formal
    comparison between the two implementations has been conducted yet.
